# OSD/OS's own addition to RetroArch 1.20.0 (commit
# ab3b175848fa6cd8b2340809631e30bc0fe1d136, the v1.20.0 tag), which
# scripts/build-retroarch.sh applies after scripts/retroarch-fixes.patch,
# before it builds the Linux arm64 package's RetroArch. OSD/OS's own, from
# no upstream commit:
#
# 1. configuration.h and configuration.c: a boolean setting,
#    osdos_system_show, false unless a configuration file sets it, so that
#    a stock configuration behaves exactly as before.
# 2. gfx/video_driver.c, video_driver_frame() and a helper before it,
#    video_driver_osdos_system(): with osdos_system_show and fps_show both
#    on, the status text carries after the frame rate the processor's load
#    in percent (all cores together, from the first line of /proc/stat,
#    over the last fps_update_interval), the temperature in degrees (the
#    first of /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0..9/temp that reads, which is
#    thermal_zone0 on a Raspberry Pi), and UNDERVOLT or THROTTLED while the
#    Raspberry Pi's firmware reports under-voltage (bit 0) or a capped
#    clock, throttling or the soft temperature limit (bits 1 to 3) now,
#    from its sysfs node get_throttled where it exists: the first
#    /sys/devices/platform/soc*/soc*:firmware/get_throttled, looked for
#    once (soc/soc:firmware on a Pi 4, under the soc's address on a Pi 5),
#    read with fopen(), no process started. The files are read when the frame rate is computed,
#    once per fps_update_interval frames, never per frame; one that can't
#    be read leaves its part out. Linux only: elsewhere the key is read and
#    the frame rate shown alone. OSD/OS writes the key for Settings ->
#    Arcade -> Show Stats' FPS + System (src/modules/arcade/Libretro.cpp,
#    configText()).
#
# A RetroArch without this patch ignores the key: config_load_file() reads
# only the settings it knows, by name. Nothing here changes RetroArch's
# version, its netplay protocol or what two machines send each other.
# Made on 2026-11-27 with diff -u against the tag with
# scripts/retroarch-fixes.patch applied; applied with patch -p1 --fuzz=0.

